==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
Confer Old English {{term|hereberga|lang=ang}}, {{term|herebeorga}}, {{term|herberowe}}, {{term|harbrough}} and {{term|herber}}. Modern English {{term|harbour|lang=en}} and {{term|arbour}}; middle High German {{term|herberge|lang=de}}; German {{term|herberge|lang=de}}; Swedish {{term|härbärge|lang=sv}}; hence Italian {{term|albergo|lang=it}} and French {{term|auberge|lang=fr}}.

===Noun===
{{non-noun|n}}

# a [[harbour]]
# an [[inn]]
# a [[closet]], a [[room]]

====Derived terms====
* [[taka sér herbergi]] (to take lodgings)

====Descendants====
* Icelandic: {{l|is|herbergi}}
* Swedish: {{l|is|härbärge}}

